'''Music Fest Thundia''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Gals of Summer Blue Ocean (Gacha Event)|Gals of Summer Blue Ocean]] gacha event. She is an anti-[[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|Angel]] variant of [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]] that was added in [[Version 13.5 Update|Version 13.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 759
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Music Fest Thundia
|name2 = Music Fest Thundia, type β
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Music Fest Thundia, type β''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Much like her [[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|other]] [[Spooky Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|variants]], Music Fest Thundia is a simple unit; she stays in the back and, if well protected, she will sometimes land a powerful attack that will heavily cripple any Angel enemy caught in the blast, all while dealing acceptable damage to other enemies.

Thankfully, she does not struggle nearly as much against her target trait as her Halloween themed predecessor does. This is because Angels tend to be tankier than [[:Category:Dark Enemies|Dark Enemies]], and as a result are much easier to clump up into large groups for her to dispose of, especially if you have access to [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Rocker Cat]] and its evolutions. Avoid using units who can knockback Angel enemies while she is out, as those Cats make a terrible synergy with Music Fest Thundia due to her lengthy foreswing.

In addition to Thundia's usual Massive damage ability, Music Fest Thundia also has a brief, yet guaranteed Freeze effect that can help supporting units push further into the enemy frontlines after she attacks. As an extra bonus, she comes pre-packaged with full Weaken immunity. While not quite as significant as say, Wave or Surge immunity, it does at least ensure that her damage output will be unaffected by the likes of [[Mr. Angel]] and [[Winged Pigge]] anytime they appear.

